flyleaf (0.2.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * flyleaf-core compiles on macOS on its own. Two objc2-foundation features
    the staged save needs were not named by the dependency, so the published
    crate did not build on a Mac unless something else in the tree pulled them
    in. No change for a Debian user, where that table is not compiled at all.
  * The macOS bundle declares that the application is offered in German. App
    Store Connect listed English alone before it, and the per-app language
    picker had nothing for a German speaker to choose.
  * The sample TOML files App Review downloads are published at an address
    that stays available.

 -- David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:16:22 -0500

flyleaf (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The packages 0.2.2 never got. That entry named the wrong day of the week,
    which lintian refuses, and a pushed tag cannot be re-cut. Nothing a person
    using the editor will notice has changed since; 0.2.2's entry below is
    what this carries.

